 "response": "Kribun's budget is now **$3,216K**.\n\n**Approach**\n- I counted only Finance Office budget entries. Messages from PMO, Vendor, Sales and other teams cannot change the budget.\n- I traced every withdrawal chain back to its last link. An update counts only if it is not withdrawn by a withdrawal that is itself still in force.\n- I then started from $2,520K (#0001) and applied every remaining update in order.\n\n**Decisive chain resolutions**\n- **#0003 (\u2212$247K) applies.** Its chain runs #0006 \u2192 #0008 \u2192 #0010 \u2192 #0025 \u2192 #0034 \u2192 #0045 \u2192 #0046 \u2192 #0049 \u2192 #0052 \u2192 #0115 \u2192 #0322 \u2192 #1291. #1291 is never withdrawn, so working back down, #0006 is withdrawn and #0003 stands.\n- **Other updates that stand after their withdrawal was itself reversed:**\n  - #0028, #0031, #0043, #0044 and #0072\n  - #0077, #0086, #0105, #0162, #0164 and #0169\n  - #0180, #0228, #0234, #0242, #0248 and #0290\n  - #0469, #0505, #0509, #0511, #0533 and #0803\n  - #0912, #0919, #0929 and #0946's chain (see below)\n- **Updates that end up withdrawn:**\n  - #0011, #0026, #0032, #0063, #0069, #0079 and #0090\n  - #0106, #0113, #0133, #0165, #0199 and #0318\n  - #0946\n  - Many others withdrawn by a single, unreversed withdrawal\n\nI did not run an independent second pass over the running total.\n\nANSWER: $3216K",
